  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "note-tweaks",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -150,
      "w": 560,
      "page": "page-1",
      "text": "Ticker desk — the tweak chips switch readState (idle · loading · trade · no_trade · stale · cooldown · signed_out · no_key), live (pulses, particles, trail), scheme (dark · light) and the phone sheet (open · peek). Click “Analyze current snapshot” to run loading → trade; Field / Magnet switches the hero. Expand this frame and resize your window: the layout is fluid."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-resp",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -150,
      "w": 620,
      "page": "page-2",
      "text": "Same source, five widths. Every frame here renders the identical page body through one set of media and container queries — nothing is redrawn by hand. The phone desk docks the AI read as a bottom sheet; tables become cards under 1000px; the settings rail becomes tabs under 900px."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-site",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -150,
      "w": 520,
      "page": "page-3",
      "text": "Site surfaces at 1440. Copy is grounded in the product (69-name universe, ~60s desk cadence, ~3-min scanner sweep, 7–45 DTE, simulated book, BYO key); all prices, P/L, scores and timestamps are sample values."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-dialogs",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -150,
      "w": 520,
      "page": "page-4",
      "text": "Every overlay and gate in the product: sign-in and the private-testing wall, the one shared sim trade-entry dialog in both variants (with the six binding disclosures verbatim), the egress drawer, persona editing, order detail in both coverage states, the scan view editor, route fallback, 404, and the two operator surfaces."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-v4-data",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -520,
      "w": 900,
      "page": "v4-data",
      "text": "v4 · Data states (2026-10-13). The hybrid site: live where free public data reaches, honestly not live where the paid options feed is needed. Source map → state matrix → the NVDA desk in both honest options (explain, or a labelled sample). Every board names the review findings it resolves (design/REVIEW-2026-10-13.md). Figures are illustrative design values."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-system",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -150,
      "w": 560,
      "page": "page-5",
      "text": "The library is generated from tokens/tokens.json and src/components — every state shown there is a registered state. The light renders prove the scheme is a token swap, not a second layout."
